    "evidence_contract": "solve_question:1",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-143677",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/7602d1695610361f28613d8bf3542056b2624f9b6b8980873f6fdebf802c6750.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$",
