    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3669",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/5a58c1b6b72ab29c73457834bd093b23df234d4b161d87b026449ce18a510cb6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/930d394a1db5ccce972522f0659cce458331e091337e8fe0816a7cb0f983ed36.svg) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/c0c348883f19c18a48444415da35aeaa27f8a18606bf5955e34aec416e248cad.svg) is a constant. Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/93ff70ccd7e98c9ff29c693618976524bac313e69ffc9bd661e452e7c5fa281e.svg) what is the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/93d1eead46fd94ca75a2cddc082709fe04b611851d408c09b77d5682f4f01711.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The parameter ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/c0c348883f19c18a48444415da35aeaa27f8a18606bf5955e34aec416e248cad.svg) represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/55272b709d4709de6420048a45c0c8303e6e0b28acfedd1f204aab4aca7ea84f.svg)\n\nThe factor ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/9fcab400c45543015fd0bbf24c9e743f9ab0664521f1a5fb346df8c6c33f2042.svg) indicates that the graph of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/822d6cbf124d2be7e2107a82106732662a98cd4436098e067e40166b82b74a7a.svg) is a horizontal translation of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/888d98ed5f0d029e400b399f96835baf53e6b4a05168e8ec4d4bdaeb41010ecd.svg) Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/4ae5b54c0b0aafdb3e191dd01d0c3ff698bda9daee3a51ad49ecf0a0313c8186.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/c5908411986cb7e8b1d5f0384086bce3c0bcc525c08738e7e8b539ea3eb883d9.svg) by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/0028652b311de658f0495a693e4be105809cdffbebc9f47c0d44a0f291c30ca4.svg) units to the right. Therefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/79f6509afbcf7d498f3a2d9e6bdcddef5af3e4a8d6a64e2517ca47bb34abc01f.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/43006dc59da6d9decabaaf78ea186ed2a2da0b20c9414d52adb77b5f56e87ed0.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/b1a26c8d2f6beaf8d1cfd2c814b7f20ddc905b4f2cf2b5d8a29b95150ebea541.svg) is in this interval, the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/c0c348883f19c18a48444415da35aeaa27f8a18606bf5955e34aec416e248cad.svg) is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260558/assets/b1a26c8d2f6beaf8d1cfd2c814b7f20ddc905b4f2cf2b5d8a29b95150ebea541.svg).",
